## Commands

### `context`

Displays the current `azd` project, environment and deployment context.

### `listen`

Starts the extension host and listens for `azd` project and service lifecycle events.

### `prompt`

Demonstrates the prompting capabilities available to extensions, including
selecting an Azure subscription, resource group and resource.

## Development

| Command | Description |
| ------- | ----------- |
| `azd x build` | Build the extension and install it locally. |
| `azd x watch` | Watch for changes and automatically rebuild and reinstall. |
| `azd x pack` | Package the extension into a distributable artifact. |
| `azd x publish` | Publish the extension to an extension source. |
| `azd x release` | Create a GitHub release for the extension. |

Learn more about building extensions in the
[azd extension framework docs](https://github.com/Azure/azure-dev/blob/main/cli/azd/docs/extensions/extension-framework.md).
